.TH PICOPINS 1 "2026-08-28" "picopins" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
picopins \- command-line GPIO pinout for the Raspberry Pi Pico
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B picopins
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ interface .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B picopins
prints a GPIO pinout and pin function guide for the Raspberry Pi Pico, Pico W,
Pico 2 and Pico 2 W.
.PP
By default it shows the GPIO names for the original Pico. Interfaces are added
by naming them, and the board is selected with one of the board options.
.SH BOARD OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-pico
Raspberry Pi Pico. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-picow
Raspberry Pi Pico W.
.TP
.B \-\-pico2
Raspberry Pi Pico 2.
.TP
.B \-\-pico2w
Raspberry Pi Pico 2 W.
.SH INTERFACES
One or more of
.BR spi ,
.BR i2c ,
.BR uart ,
.B pwm
and
.BR hstx .
.B hstx
is available on the Pico 2 and Pico 2 W only.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Show every interface available on the selected board.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-pins
Show physical pin numbers alongside the GPIO names.
.TP
.B \-\-hide\-gpio
Hide the GPIO names.
.TP
.B \-\-internal
List the pins wired to onboard hardware, such as the LED, the VBUS and VSYS
sense pins and, on the wireless boards, the WL_GPIO pins.
.TP
.B \-\-testpads
List the test pads on the underside of the board.
.TP
.B \-\-light
Use a light colour scheme.
.TP
.BI \-\-find " text"
Highlight pins whose labels match
.IR text ,
which may be a regular expression.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B picopins
Basic GPIO pinout for the Pico.
.TP
.B picopins i2c
GPIO names with I2C labels.
.TP
.B picopins \-\-pico2w \-\-all
Every interface, for a Pico 2 W.
.TP
.B picopins \-\-picow \-\-internal
What the Pico W wires up itself.
.TP
.B picopins \-\-all \-\-find "PWM.* A"
Highlight every PWM channel A label.
.SH SEE ALSO
The interactive pinouts at https://pico.pinout.xyz,
https://picow.pinout.xyz, https://pico2.pinout.xyz and
https://pico2w.pinout.xyz.
